model.en:
const module = await Test.createTestingModule({
  providers: [
    UsersService,
    {
      provide: getRepositoryToken(User),
      useValue: { findOne: jest.fn(), create: jest.fn((d) => d), save: jest.fn() },
    },
  ],
}).compile();

service = module.get(UsersService);
const repo = module.get(getRepositoryToken(User));

Why: drop both TypeOrmModule imports — they're what opens the real pool. Declare UsersService as the real provider and supply the repository as a useValue double keyed by getRepositoryToken(User), the exact token @InjectRepository(User) resolves to. Each method is a jest.fn() you can program (repo.findOne.mockResolvedValue(...)) and assert against. No connection opens, so the test is fast and can't flake on a pool timeout. (If you must keep imports: [UsersModule], use .overrideProvider(getRepositoryToken(User)).useValue(mock) instead.)

